# ─── .NET build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
*.user

# ─── NuGet package output & local feed ───────────────────────────────
artifacts/
local-feed/
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# ─── OS / editor cruft ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

# ─── DocFX generated output ───────────────────────────────────────────
docfx/_site/
docfx/api/

# ─── Local git worktrees ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.worktrees/

# Assistant tooling scratch - SDD task briefs and reports, 194 files on 2026-08-15.
# It WAS already ignored, but only by a nested `.superpowers/sdd/.gitignore` containing `*`,
# which covers everything under sdd/ and NOTHING ELSE. A sibling directory - `.superpowers/notes/`,
# say - would have been untracked and visible to `git add -A` in a PUBLIC repository. This rule
# covers the whole tree whatever is added inside it. Verified with `git check-ignore -v`.
.superpowers/

# Kept local, never published. These are working material for whoever is developing
# this package - design docs, the original proof-of-concept spike, and the assistant
# guidance file - not something a consumer of the NuGet package needs. They still
# exist on a maintainer's disk; they simply stop being pushed. Git history retains
# every version committed before this point.
docs/
spike/
CLAUDE.md
# Paired with CLAUDE.md and ignored for the same reason: it is guidance for whoever
# develops this package, not for a consumer of the NuGet package. It moved here from
# docs/ on 2026-08-15 so it sits beside CLAUDE.md, which cites it - and it needs its
# OWN rule now, because docs/ above is no longer what covers it.
SOURCE-QUALITY.md

# Mutation-testing reports. Regenerated on every run; the score is the artefact
# that matters and CI uploads it.
StrykerOutput/

# Benchmark output. Regenerated on every run; the uploaded artifact is the record.
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/

# Coverage reports. Same reasoning as the two above, and the same shape of artifact:
# ci.yml collects them here (--results-directory) and uploads the directory. Reproducing
# that run locally, which is the only way to check the coverage gate before pushing, left
# them untracked rather than ignored - so `git add -A` would have swept a pile of
# cobertura XML into a commit.
TestResults/

# Architecture decision records. Kept on disk alongside CLAUDE.md and docs/, not published.
adr/
